--- log ---
2026-09-14T05:30Z claude created
2026-09-14T05:31Z claude note Filed from the decorrelated review of PR #554, which raised it as a structural concern the PR neither tested nor discussed. The reviewer could not confirm it live for the same reason PR #554's own probe could not read tab order — no X focus on the test display, and no xdotool on the host — so this is filed as an open question with the evidence that motivates it, not as a confirmed defect. Filing it rather than fixing it because the remedy is not obvious: it may be an attribute, or it may be an entry in a Zotero map this add-on has no business writing into.

2026-09-14T10:30Z claude note ANSWERED, and the answer is the bad one: the control is NOT reachable by Tab. Measured on the author's own desktop, him at the keyboard, because no synthetic route could take the reading -- `sendNativeKeyEvent` is inert in this build, shown by a positive control where a plain character key never reached a focused search box. So he pressed Tab and the session sampled `document.activeElement`. THE CONTROL FIRED: focus travelled through some sixty distinct elements -- item tree, item pane fields, creator rows, attachment preview, sync, collections -- so Tab was demonstrably working and the null is a real null. `sdt-pack-sitter-button` never appeared, and the author confirms from the screen that the Index button never highlighted. The sharpest detail: `zotero-tb-add`, a button in the SAME zotero-items-toolbar, WAS reached. So it is not that toolbar buttons are unreachable; it is that the ones named in `setUpKeyboardNavigation`'s id-keyed map are reachable and ours is not. Exactly what review predicted from reading omni.ja. Focusable and reachable were never the same claim; tabindex="0" bought the first and not the second. RELEASE-NOTES.md corrected in the same commit: it promised keyboard operation a user will not get. The remedy stays open -- this ticket's invariant still says writing our id into Zotero's own pane map is not obviously ours to do.

2026-09-14T10:34Z MinhHaDuong ruled NO WORKAROUND. Zotero's toolbar keyboard navigation is closed to plugins -- the actionsMap is local to setUpKeyboardNavigation() -- and that is upstream's gap, not this add-on's. A keyboard shortcut was proposed and refused: asking a user to learn a keybinding to reach a button is not accessibility, it only moves the cost onto them. tabindex="0" stays, since it costs nothing and lets a screen reader move focus directly. This ticket becomes an upstream report rather than a fix.

2026-09-14T19:29Z claude note REPORTED UPSTREAM by the author, in his own name: https://forums.zotero.org/discussion/133759/plugin-toolbar-buttons-are-still-outside-the-keyboard-navigation-chain , filed as a follow-up to forum discussion 97505 rather than as a new claim -- dstillman wrote there on 2023-02-23 that 'In Zotero 6.0.22, available now, all toolbar buttons are accessible via the keyboard', which is true of the NATIVE buttons and leaves plugin-contributed ones outside. The mechanism in the report was verified against zoteroPane.js in the shipped omni.ja rather than taken from this ticket: setUpKeyboardNavigation() builds each actionsMap as a `let` inside its own keydown callback, moveFocus looks up actionsMap[event.target.id] and then falls back over event.target.classList, and all nineteen top-level keys are Zotero's own element ids or specific Zotero classes (zotero-tb-add, zotero-tb-sync, search-input, tag-selector-list and so on). The classList fallback looked at first like a way in for a plugin and is not, because no generic 'a toolbar button' key exists -- so the report ASKS for a hook (a recognised class, or a registration call) instead of asserting the case is hopeless, and offers to test a patch. The author's ruling of 2026-09-14 stands unchanged: asking a user to learn a shortcut is not a solution, and nothing is worked around on our side.
2026-09-16T11:00Z claude note Author ruling 2026-09-16: forum thread 133759 drew no reply, convert to a Zotero PR. This one asked for a hook rather than carrying one, which GOVERNANCE would have called design-sized; that rule is zoteus-shaped and does not reach Zotero, so the PR must propose the minimal API itself (a recognised class, or a registration call) against setUpKeyboardNavigation in zoteroPane.js. Not started, by the author's instruction.
